    <p>Push a malformed update to crash the widget, then try to bring it back. In broken mode, nothing works except reloading the page. In fixed mode, watch "Try again" actually attempt a fresh render — and actually fail again if the data's still bad.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>Broken mode's fallback state never changes once <code>hasError</code> is true, no matter what button you click. Fixed mode's "Try again" clears that flag and re-renders the real children, so it succeeds or fails based on the data at that exact moment.</p>
