{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A boundary that catches an error but never gets a reason to try again will show the same fallback forever, even after the real problem is gone — recovery needs an explicit reset path, not just a catch.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Wire a key change, a resetKeys array, or an explicit reset callback into every error boundary that's meant to recover, not just contain — a caught error with no way back is a permanent one.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Reset on a real changed signal (a connection ID, a request ID, a resetKeys entry that isn't recomputed every render) rather than an unconditional timer, and remember the boundary only ever covers render-phase errors in descendants, not event handlers or async callbacks.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
